<body class="marketing-page">
	<SiteNav />

	<main>

	<section class="hero alt-hero">
		<div class="hero-badge">Alternatives · Self-Hosted</div>
		<h1>The Mailcow alternative<br/><span>built for operators.</span></h1>
		<p class="alt-lead">
			Both are self-hosted Docker stacks on the same Postfix/Dovecot/Rspamd core.
			The difference is the operating model: Vectis Mail runs from a single declarative
			<code>config.yaml</code>, a Go REST API, and atomic updates with health-gated
			rollback — where Mailcow leans on a bash env file, a web UI, and a manual
			<code>update.sh</code>. Same self-hosted control, driven as code.
		</p>
		<div class="hero-buttons" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
			<a href="/getting-started/installation/" class="btn-primary">Install Vectis Mail free</a>
			<a href="/pricing/" class="btn-secondary">View pricing</a>
